   ],
   "design": "The ground station records the scanned sonde serial, launch time and surface observations, so the meteorologist adds only remarks to the launch log. The ground station codes the sounding message from the received data, and the meteorologist checks it before it is sent. Quality records and the monthly report come from the station's own data, with the measured values, not planned ones. Preparing, launching, monitoring, maintenance, checking, sending and orders stay with the meteorologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Serials, times and data were written and coded by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Ground station software that records, codes and reports from the sounding data.",
   "still_hard": "Failed launches in strong wind.",
   "human_edge": "Judging when the wind makes a launch unsafe.",
